alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The properties_tables entry, invoked as `properties_tables DIR` with DIR naming, relative to the working directory, a directory holding the Unicode 17.0.0 character database files DerivedGeneralCategory.txt and emoji-data.txt. It reads every code point's General_Category from DerivedGeneralCategory.txt, defaulting to Cn where the file does not otherwise cover it, and every code point's Extended_Pictographic from emoji-data.txt, and packs the two into one byte per code point: General_Category's 0-based index in the Unicode Standard's listed order (Lu, Ll, Lt, Lm, Lo, Mn, Mc, Me, Nd, Nl, No, Pc, Pd, Ps, Pe, Pi, Pf, Po, Sm, Sc, Sk, So, Zs, Zl, Zp, Cc, Cf, Cs, Co, Cn) in the low 5 bits, Extended_Pictographic in bit 7. It prints to standard output the Whitefoot source of two const arrays, a two-stage block table over the 1,114,112 code points: gc_block_index, one entry per 256-code-point block naming which deduplicated 256-byte block holds its bytes, and gc_block_bytes, each distinct block's packed bytes once, so a lookup is one block-index read and one packed-byte read. It exits 0 after printing, 1 when an argument is missing, and 2 when a file cannot be read.";
